{"abstract":"Very few forests take up as much space in contemporary Western imagination as the Amazon. It is the archetypical mythological forest that many people want to save and even more people want to exploit. Over the years, it has been the object of multiple campaigns to ‘save the rainforest’ from resource extraction both within South America and beyond, within scientific communities as well as broader publics. This article addresses a concern with how to extract the resources of the Amazon Forest in ways that are more sustainable than past and contemporary logging, mining and farming. This concern is promoted by Brazilian scientists who have allied themselves with well-intended tech industry initiatives and small-scale entrepreneurs. We refer to this combination of conservation with extraction as salvage technoscience, an approach currently dominating the struggle for the resources of the Amazon by attempting to reconcile the opposing views of the forest as an economic asset and as an object to be preserved. Our contribution thus demonstrates the interwoven nature of capitalist extraction and environmental conservation under the auspices of technoscientific progress.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Santos da Costa, Priscila","Dalsgaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754072"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Amazon Forest","Environmental conservation","Salvage Technoscience","Sustainable Resource Extraction","Technoscientific Progress"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"salvage technoscience conserving and extracting the value of the amazon rainforest","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105843079/Salvage_Technoscience_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754072","ids":["itu-58b977af-421f-4a2f-8a16-08ce0950c4ce"],"keyword":["Amazon Forest","Environmental Conservation","Salvage Technoscience","Sustainable Resource Extraction","Technoscientific Progress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FC50CB4B508150101576AF5FBD47358A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105843079/Salvage_Technoscience_accepted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Priscila","key":"santosdacostapau","last":"Santos da Costa","locid":"9734ef6f-09d1-4ca1-b968-6ad34872d504","name":"Santos da Costa, Priscila","orcid":"0000-0003-2439-9960","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/26349825241248845","issn":["26349825"],"journal":"Environment and Planning F","publisher":"Sage Publishing","status":"p","title":"Environment and Planning F"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-58b977af-421f-4a2f-8a16-08ce0950c4ce"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Salvage technoscience: Conserving and extracting the value of the Amazon Rainforest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754072","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This one-day workshop brings together Brazilian anthropologist Priscila Santos da Costa and Italian artist Sergio Racanati, to explore, both critically and creatively, different research practices engaging the forest, and more particularly the Amazon forest, as a multidimensional articulation – imaginary, real, cultural and economic. The work of Priscila Santos da Costa, based at IT University in Copenhagen, analyzes the intricate relationships between technoscientific approaches to the forest and its resources, often branded as sustainable, and capitalist modes of extraction of materials and knowledges. The question of epistemic extractivism – and the shaping of imaginative modes of relationship with the forest and its human and beyond-human inhabitants – is also at stake in Sergio Racanati’s artistic research around the notion of ‘debris’. In 2022, thanks to the support of the Italian Council, the artist spent a period of time working in the Amazon region, close to the city of Santarém, in the Brazilian state of Pará.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Santos da Costa, Priscila"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764508"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-21","place":"Lisboa, pt","start":"2023-09-21","title":"Envisioning a Forest","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Amazon Forest","Art","Science","Sustainability","Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"imaginários socio tecnológicos e a amazônia brasileira socio technical imaginaries and the brazilian amazon","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-764508","ids":["itu-85af040b-fd43-44e5-970a-7a05fd1bf61d"],"keyword":["amazon forest","art","science","sustainability","technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A193541019425A913D61E620B7074ACD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Priscila","key":"santosdacostapau","last":"Santos da Costa","locid":"9734ef6f-09d1-4ca1-b968-6ad34872d504","name":"Santos da Costa, Priscila","orcid":"0000-0003-2439-9960","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-85af040b-fd43-44e5-970a-7a05fd1bf61d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Imaginários Socio-tecnológicos e a Amazônia Brasileira : Socio-technical imaginaries and the Brazilian Amazon","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764508","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This paper focuses on the initial phase of the Covid-19 pandemic in Papua New Guinea (March to September 2020), and the government’s response to the crisis. In examining on the one hand inadequate infrastructures, an insufficient healt system, law enforcement agencies afflicted by corruption and the us of brutality, and on the other the customs and traditions of Papua New Guineans, the authors conclude that the lockdowns and social distancing measures implemented around the world are not likely to be successful in Papua New Guinea. They point out that the Covid-19 issue in Papua New Guinea reveals an «already there» state of precarity that makes the distinction «now» and «then» of affluent countries meaningless. The normalcy that characterizes liberal democratic capitalism, or life without instability or precarity, is not normalcy in Papua New Guinea, where indeterminacy is less the exception than the prevailing condition of the times. At least Covid-19 has brought these inequalities starkly into view.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Santos da Costa, Priscila","Kenema, Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382040"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of St Andrews"],"keyword":["COVID 19 pandemic","Government response","Infrastructure inadequacy","Papua New Guinea","Precarity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"precarity and the state the arrival of covid 000000000019 in papua new guinea","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86796020/14_kenema_dacosta.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S0