{"abstract":"Endemic corruption and fervent Christianity dominate Papua New Guinea (PNG) public discourse. We draw on ethnographic material—including the emplacement of a King James V Bible in Parliament—to contextualise corruption discourse and Christian measures against corruption within evolving Papua New Guinean ideas about witnessing. Both corruption discourse and Christianity invoke a specific kind of observer: a disembodied, reliable witness capable of discerning people's intentions. Established ethnographic and linguistic data from PNG meanwhile document witnesses as imagined to be embodied, interested, lacking a privileged relationship to truth, and thus susceptible to coercion. Recasting the PNG corruption issue in terms of witnessing foregrounds a perceived cultural conflict between inclusion and duty; it also reveals how and why the Christian God was invoked—using debt and obligation rhetoric—to end corruption at the national scale.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pickles, Anthony J.","Santos da Costa, Priscila"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384633"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of East Anglia"],"keyword":["Christianity","Corruption","Papua New Guinea","Politics","Social change","Witnessing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"it is christ or corruption in papua new guinea bring in the witness","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ocea.5315","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384633","identifier":[{"id":"85116923630","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e4bee173-dd90-431c-b542-fda68e9627a1"],"keyword":["Christianity","Papua New Guinea","corruption","politics","social change","witnessing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-FC50DDC51106D678751B5ED716258D58"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86612419/Oceania_2021_Pickles_It_is_Christ_or_Corruption_in_Papua_New_Guinea_Bring_in_the_Witness.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ocea.5315","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of east anglia","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of East Anglia","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anthony J.","key":"picklespau","last":"Pickles","name":"Pickles, Anthony J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Priscila","key":"santosdacostapau","last":"Santos da Costa","locid":"9734ef6f-09d1-4ca1-b968-6ad34872d504","name":"Santos da Costa, Priscila","orcid":"0000-0003-2439-9960","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ocea.5315","issn":["00298077","18344461"],"issn_org":["00298077"],"journal":"Oceania","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Oceania"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116923630"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e4bee173-dd90-431c-b542-fda68e9627a1"],"src":